    "category": "60V Power Shovel, 12 in., Brushless",
    "description": "Toro's battery Power Shovel is the cordless version of a tool Toro has sold in corded form for years, and on paper it matches the EGO closely. Toro lists a 12-inch clearing width and a 6-inch intake height, and rates it to throw snow up to 25 feet, with the usual note that distance varies with conditions. It uses a brushless motor and two speeds. Toro's listing for the 39909 kit includes a 60V MAX 2.5Ah battery and quotes up to 45 minutes of run time on a charge, with a 60-minute recharge. Toro also sells a bare-tool version, 39909T, without the battery; check the suffix before you buy, because the two are easy to confuse on retailer pages. The case for it is the platform: Toro's Flex-Force 60V batteries also run its mowers, trimmers and battery snow blowers, covered in our <a href=\"/toro-electric-snow-blower/\">Toro electric snow blower guide</a>. If you own none of those, it is a closer call against the EGO.",
    "pros": [
      "12-inch width and 6-inch intake, per Toro",
      "Rated throw up to 25 feet",
      "Kit includes a 2.5Ah battery; Toro quotes up to 45 minutes",
      "Brushless motor with two speeds",
      "Shares batteries with Toro's 60V Flex-Force lineup"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Easy to buy the bare 39909T by mistake",
      "Run-time figure is for light snow in mild cold",
      "No wheels"
    ],
