          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-of/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Best Cordless Snow Shovels",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-cordless-snow-shovel/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the best cordless snow shovel?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For most people the EGO 56V 12-inch shovel is the best all-rounder: EGO rates it to throw snow up to 25 feet with a 60-degree directional dial, and lists it at 16.7 pounds with its recommended battery. But if you already own Toro, Greenworks, Ryobi or DeWalt batteries, the bare shovel on your existing platform is usually the better value."
