            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Look for the lightest tool you can find, and wheels if you have a long walk. The Snow Joe 24V-SS13-XR is the lightest complete kit here at a listed 13.5 to 14 pounds, and Ryobi's 40V wheeled shovel lets you push rather than carry. Anyone with heart or back concerns should check with a doctor first."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a battery snow shovel run?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the battery and the snow. Toro quotes up to 45 minutes on a 2.5Ah battery and DeWalt about 20 minutes on 4Ah, both in favourable conditions. Cold batteries and wet snow cut that substantially. Keeping the battery warm until use and having a second pack are the most reliable ways to extend it."
