            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long does a battery snow shovel run?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It depends on the battery and the snow. Toro quotes up to 45 minutes on a 2.5Ah battery and DeWalt about 20 minutes on 4Ah, both in favourable conditions. Cold batteries and wet snow cut that substantially. Keeping the battery warm until use and having a second pack are the most reliable ways to extend it.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the Greenworks 80V snow shovel worth it?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It is a good buy if you already own Greenworks 80V tools. Greenworks lists a 12-inch path and 6-inch depth with a brushless motor, and an LED variant is listed at an 8-inch depth. Listed run time and throw distance vary between sellers, and the higher voltage does not widen the intake, so it is not worth switching platforms for.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a cordless snow shovel clear a driveway?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                A short single-car driveway in light snow, yes, if you go out early and often. A two-car or longer driveway means many passes at 10 to 13 inches each, and the plow berm will stop it. For a full driveway, a battery snow blower on the same platform is the better main tool.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Does EGO make a standalone snow shovel or just an attachment?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Both. EGO sells a standalone 56V 12-inch snow shovel, SNS1201 as a kit or SNS1200 bare, and a separate SSA1200 snow shovel attachment for its Multi-Head power head. EGO lists the attachment with a 12-inch width, up to 25 feet of throw and a 5-year warranty. If you already own the Multi-Head, the attachment is cheaper.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
